course: dictionary
lesson: 4726
title: Hopper: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hopper is a word you may know from hop. A grasshopper is a hopper because it hops. But a hopper can also be a big container on a farm or in a factory, so you need the context to know which meaning fits.
explain: «Frozen pizzas get toppings from machines, sometimes falling like snow from hoppers» tells you that the toppings fall out of the hopper. Things cannot fall out of an insect, so this hopper must be a container. Always ask: does my meaning fit the sentence?
explain: Look for clues like capital letters. In «Grace Hopper was a computing pioneer», the capital H shows that Hopper is a person's name. Names are not containers or insects, so when you see a capital letter in the middle of a sentence, think about names.
fact: A hopper is a large container shaped like a funnel, which lets grain, coal, sand or food pour out at the bottom.
fact: A hopper can also be a person, animal or insect that hops, such as a grasshopper.
fact: «Hopper» can be a name: Grace Hopper was a famous American computer scientist, and Edward Hopper was a painter.
fact: In the phrase «in the hopper» (US), something is waiting to be dealt with.
exercise: «Grain poured from the hopper into the waiting truck.» What is a hopper here? | A jumping insect | A farm dog | A kind of computer | *A large funnel-shaped container for grain
exercise: «The grasshopper leapt across the grass.» What kind of hopper is this? | *A creature that hops | A container for coal | A famous painter | A machine that makes pizza
exercise: «In 1947 Grace Hopper's team found a real moth in a computer.» What kind of word is Hopper in this sentence? | An insect | *A person's name | A type of grain | A container
test: Someone who moves quickly from place to place, like a «bar-hopper», is called a hopper in an informal way. What does hopper mean in «bar-hopper»? | *Someone who moves quickly from place to place | A frog | A computer | A large container for drinks
test: «Programmers have called faults bugs for a long time.» What did Grace Hopper's team find in a computer in 1947? | Toppings | Grain | Coal | *A real moth
exam: Which sentence uses hopper as a name? | Grain fell from the hopper. | *Edward Hopper painted many pictures of American city life. | A hopper jumped over the fence. | The hopper was full of coal.
